  READ THIS AS: the paper claims p is identifiable up to a STABLE calibratable
  attenuation. Monotone recovery in every cell supports the first half. The second
  half needs the slope to be about the same across targets and grids, since a
  calibration that depends on the unknown density is not available in practice. If
  the slope spread is large, or a single pooled calibration leaves errors in p of
  more than a few hundredths, the sentence should be narrowed to monotonicity.

